From: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mali_kbase: port to 7.0.12-cix-sky1-next + fix 2 probe-time
 NULL-pointer-deref panics found on real hardware

Consolidated provenance patch (squash of 5 working commits made against
ARM's cix_p1_mg_dev tree, base commit a752e91 "Cix p1 mg 202603 patch
release") documenting the full port of the CIX Sky1 Mali-G720
out-of-tree GPU kernel module (mali_kbase / memory_group_manager /
protected_memory_allocator) from the 7.2.0-rc4-sky1-ncz kernel (where
it already ships as the validated default GPU driver) to the older
7.0.12-cix-sky1-next kernel (our LTS/emergency-fallback channel, where
in-tree panthor is the current validated default -- see
docs/DRIVER_FIDELITY_7012.md). This is NOT a default-driver change;
see dkms.conf for scope/status.

What's in this squash, in the order it was actually done:

1. Kernel-API port (reference patches 0002-0007, 0009, 0011-0013 from
   the sibling 7.2 port, applied against this older-numbered kernel
   where the same root causes are present): Kbuild srctree/src path
   normalization, mm_get_unmapped_area() 5-arg signature,
   hrtimer_setup(), dma_fence_ops.fence_value_str, shmem vma_flags_t,
   timer_delete rename, dma_fence_signal() void return.

2. Two 7.0.12-specific compat guards, gated on a new
   MALI_KBASE_TARGETS_7_0_12_CIX_SKY1_NEXT_BACKPORT macro
   (LINUX_VERSION_CODE == KERNEL_VERSION(7,0,12), deliberately narrow
   so it cannot misfire on other 7.0.x/7.1.x kernels):
     - version_compat_defs.h: this kernel independently backported the
       mainline-7.2 page-movable-ops rework (Sky1-Linux community
       patch "mm: add Mali GPU movable_ops page type support") but
       LINUX_VERSION_CODE still reads 7.0.12, so the existing >= 7.2.0
       guard on the __SetPageMovable()/__ClearPageMovable() no-op shim
       never fired. Widened to also fire for this exact kernel.
     - mali_kbase_config_sky1.c: this kernel's
       drivers/pmdomain/arm/scmi_perf_domain.c predates
       scmi_device_opp_table_parse() (added later, in the ncz72 BSP
       branch's rewrite of that driver); fall back to
       dev_pm_opp_get_opp_count() directly instead.

3. Independent adversarial (Codex) review of (2) above requested two
   follow-ups, both applied: centralize the version-tuple check in
   mali_kbase_fence_ops.c through the one macro instead of re-deriving
   it inline in 3 places; add unique grep-able dmesg markers
   (SKY1_7_0_12_OPP_MISSING / OPP table already populated) around the
   SCMI-OPP fallback so a silently-DVFS-disabled A/B test run can't be
   mistaken for a real comparison.

4. Ported mali-kbase-scmi-ratelimit.patch (../../mali/mali-kbase-scmi-ratelimit.patch,
   already shipping in the 7.2 driver) unchanged into
   mali_kbase_devfreq.c: kernel-version-independent devfreq logic
   (100ms SCMI rate limit, dedup on last-set freq, error backoff +
   safe-freq boost, always return 0 from the devfreq target callback).
   Applied reactively, not proactively -- see item 5.

5. Two real, reproducible NULL/garbage-pointer-deref kernel panics
   found via LIVE HARDWARE TESTING on cixmini (.66, 2026-07-27), both
   root-caused from a pstore/ramoops-captured crash dump after the
   board auto-rebooted (panic=30):

     Unable to handle kernel NULL pointer dereference at virtual
     address 00000000000001af ... FSC = 0x21: alignment fault
     pc : __pm_runtime_resume+0x34/0xa8
     lr : device_link_add+0x2f0/0x710
     kbase_platform_sky1_init+0x68/0x2f8 [mali_kbase]

   sky1_gpu_attach_pd() in mali_kbase_config_sky1.c calls
   device_link_add() twice -- once for the "perf" SCMI power domain,
   once for the ACPI "power-supply" device -- and in BOTH cases passed
   the attach result straight to device_link_add() with no NULL/ERR
   check, even though dev_pm_domain_attach_by_name() /
   fwnode_dev_pm_domain_attach_by_name() / bus_find_device_by_fwnode()
   can all legitimately return NULL, and device_link_add() derefs its
   supplier internally. Reproduced identically twice (crash #1 fixed
   the power-supply call site only; crash #2, an IDENTICAL trace,
   showed the *first* device_link_add() call -- the "perf" one -- was
   the actual hit, not yet guarded). Fixed both call sites with an
   IS_ERR_OR_NULL() check returning -EPROBE_DEFER, matching the
   existing IS_ERR_OR_NULL(fwnode) error style a few lines above.

   Status after fix: mali_kbase.ko now loads WITHOUT crashing the
   board (verified: insmod succeeds, board stays up, confirmed via
   dmesg "perf power-domain device not bound yet, deferring probe").
   However probe does not complete -- the "perf" SCMI power-domain
   device this driver expects apparently never binds on this kernel's
   ACPI/pm_domain topology (checked /sys/kernel/debug/devices_deferred:
   CIXH5000:00 sits there persistently, not a transient race), so
   /dev/mali0 never appears. NOT YET FUNCTIONAL as a GPU driver --
   safe to load, but no GPU device node. Root-causing why the "perf"
   power domain never binds on 7.0.12 (vs. 7.2, where it does) is
   follow-up work; see dkms.conf and docs/DRIVER_FIDELITY_7012.md.

Build validated (cixmini, 7.0.12-cix-sky1-next headers):
mali_kbase.ko + memory_group_manager.ko + protected_memory_allocator.ko
all build clean, vermagic "7.0.12-cix-sky1-next SMP preempt mod_unload
aarch64".

Signed-off-by: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/base/arm/Kbuild b/drivers/base/arm/Kbuild
index 80f1a6b..468bd2e 100644
--- a/drivers/base/arm/Kbuild
+++ b/drivers/base/arm/Kbuild
@@ -25,8 +25,12 @@ endif
 #
 # ccflags
 #
-src:=$(if $(patsubst /%,,$(src)),$(srctree)/$(src),$(src))
-ccflags-y += -I$(src)/../../../include
+# Use $(M) (KBUILD_EXTMOD), not $(srctree)-relative $(src): on kernels
+# where $(srctree) resolves to the kernel tree rather than this
+# out-of-tree module's own tree, the old $(srctree)-based
+# reconstruction points at the wrong directory. $(M) is always this
+# module's absolute invocation directory regardless of kernel version.
+ccflags-y += -I$(M)/../../../include
 
 subdir-ccflags-y += $(ccflags-y)
 
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/Kbuild b/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/Kbuild
index bb5855f..c9ec324 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/Kbuild
+++ b/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/Kbuild
@@ -18,9 +18,15 @@
 #
 #
 
-# make $(src) as absolute path if it is not already, by prefixing $(srctree)
-# This is to prevent any build issue due to wrong path.
-src:=$(if $(patsubst /%,,$(src)),$(srctree)/$(src),$(src))
+# make $(src) as absolute path if it is not already, by prefixing $(M)
+# (KBUILD_EXTMOD, this out-of-tree module's own absolute invocation
+# directory). $(srctree) is the KERNEL source tree for an external
+# module build, not this module's tree, so prefixing with $(srctree)
+# resolves to the wrong location on kernels where $(src) starts as the
+# relative "." case. $(M) is always this module's own absolute path
+# regardless of kernel version. This is to prevent any build issue due
+# to wrong path.
+src:=$(if $(patsubst /%,,$(src)),$(M)/$(src),$(src))
 
 #
 # Prevent misuse when Kernel configurations are not present by default
